{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out","id":1188322,"title":"Anyone had a bygone familiar? How did it work out?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-21T15:53:19-08:00","id":1188322,"title":"Anyone had a bygone familiar? How did it work out?","content":"Having a griffon, dragon or what have you sounds cool as hell, but I just don't see how it can work unless you start a game with characters that are much more advanced than normal starting characters.<br /> <br /> You need regular access to a powerful node in order to supply them with quintessence. And there's the problem of paradox. Anyone sees you with your pet monster and you get hit with paradox.<br /> <br /> One thing I did think of was a bygone with a charm that allows them to shapeshift from an innocous form to battle form. If anyone has seen Inuyasha, I'm thinking of the way Sango's cat which goes from a cute kitten with two tails (animals are born with defects like two heads sometimes, so that's easy to brush off as coincendental) to a giant sabertooth cat that can fly.<br /> <br /> But that assumes a homebrewed bygone. Griffon's and most other famous monsters don't shapeshift. And while in some myths Dragons do, dragons already tend to be way overpowered.<br /> <br /> Are these problems easier to get around then I'm assuming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":".  Terrible typo 03-11-2018, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T16:02:12-08:00","id":1188324,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure, but remember: technomancers have robots as familiars all the time and they're technically bygones, so there has to be <i>some </i>way to make them useful without being a paradox magnet or just leaving them in the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T16:41:50-08:00","id":1188335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188324#post1188324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure, but remember: technomancers have robots as familiars all the time and they're technically bygones, so there has to be <i>some </i>way to make them useful without being a paradox magnet or just leaving them in the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Robot Familiars are constructs. They aren't a paradox magnet because people believe in Robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T17:04:41-08:00","id":1188341,"title":"","content":"Then why do HIT Marks attract paradox? I feel like most robots that could reasonably be familiars are advanced enough to count as violations of the consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T17:32:53-08:00","id":1188349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188341#post1188341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why do HIT Marks attract paradox? I feel like most robots that could reasonably be familiars are advanced enough to count as violations of the consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hit marks generally pass for human and don't attract paradox.<br /> <br /> That being said here are the rules for Paradox and Familiars. IF they do something infront of Sleepers that's outside bounds, so Cat talks infront of sleeper, you get one paradox. Dragon shows up infront of sleeper 1 paradox. I am not sure what sort of act would count to show a machine is &quot;too advanced&quot; infront of sleepers but there you go.<br /> <br /> Generally Technomancers either keep their toys in their labs or they conceal them. IF you want a Bygone Familiar have it take the invisibility charm then you are good, or have it be small enough you can keep it hidden.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T17:59:23-08:00","id":1188358,"title":"","content":"AFAIC, anything above &quot;walk over uneven terrain&quot; or &quot;mimic human facial expressions&quot; is past what the consensus can handle right now. Certainly, anything that could be reliably useful for anything other than fetching small objects would be vulgar. Kinda' like how a lot of people believe in the divine, but would still count as disbelievers for a miracle worker, a lot of people know that advanced robotics are probably in development <i>somewhere</i>, but would still be incredulous to actually <i>see </i>one in person outside a science museum or a tech expo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T18:13:36-08:00","id":1188360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188358#post1188358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIC, anything above &quot;walk over uneven terrain&quot; or &quot;mimic human facial expressions&quot; is past what the consensus can handle right now. Certainly, anything that could be reliably useful for anything other than fetching small objects would be vulgar. Kinda' like how a lot of people believe in the divine, but would still count as disbelievers for a miracle worker, a lot of people know that advanced robotics are probably in development <i>somewhere</i>, but would still be incredulous to actually <i>see </i>one in person outside a science museum or a tech expo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, seeing youtube videos from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fRj34o4hN4I\" target=\"_blank\">Boston Dynamic</a> is not the same as watching the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_cwaxfa0JUE\" target=\"_blank\">Destroyer</a> robot from Thor tear the town up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 02-21-2018, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T18:18:02-08:00","id":1188362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188360#post1188360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, seeing youtube videos from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fRj34o4hN4I\" target=\"_blank\">Boston Dynamic</a> is not the same as watching the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_cwaxfa0JUE\" target=\"_blank\">Destroyer</a> robot for Thor tear the town up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And I'd even argue that seeing Atlas outside a very specific context (e.g. a lab or a tech demo, i.e. a hypertech-friendly reality zone) would still accrue 'dox (though not nearly as much, obviously).<br /> <br /> The moral of the story is that Sleepers suck and hate fun. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T18:30:56-08:00","id":1188363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188358#post1188358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIC, anything above &quot;walk over uneven terrain&quot; or &quot;mimic human facial expressions&quot; is past what the consensus can handle right now. Certainly, anything that could be reliably useful for anything other than fetching small objects would be vulgar. Kinda' like how a lot of people believe in the divine, but would still count as disbelievers for a miracle worker, a lot of people know that advanced robotics are probably in development <i>somewhere</i>, but would still be incredulous to actually <i>see </i>one in person outside a science museum or a tech expo.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being beyond human tech will not be an &quot;auto paradox&quot; the irony here being the more informed a person is about tech the more likely they are to be a problematic sleeper. Everyone knows cats can't talk not everyone knows you can't make C3peo.<br /> <br /> Especially if I went with a nonhumanoid form like Smartphone, or drone, or R2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T18:52:09-08:00","id":1188365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188363#post1188363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Being beyond human tech will not be an &quot;auto paradox&quot; the irony here being the more informed a person is about tech the more likely they are to be a problematic sleeper. Everyone knows cats can't talk not everyone knows you can't make C3peo.<br /> <br /> Especially if I went with a nonhumanoid form like Smartphone, or drone, or R2.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm pretty sure people would know if your drone was doing anything more complicated than hovering close to something that something was up. Again, just because has never actively thought to themselves &quot;we are not at a point technologically where realistic and nuanced simulation of humanoid behavior and movement are possible&quot; doesn't believe that they wouldn't be flabbergasted to see it.<br /> <br /> Just because someone believes a killbot is more possible than a manticore doesn't mean that they ever expect to see one, or even think it's particularly realistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:21:11-08:00","id":1188374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188365#post1188365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm pretty sure people would know if your drone was doing anything more complicated than hovering close to something that something was up. Again, just because has never actively thought to themselves &quot;we are not at a point technologically where realistic and nuanced simulation of humanoid behavior and movement are possible&quot; doesn't believe that they wouldn't be flabbergasted to see it.<br /> <br /> Just because someone believes a killbot is more possible than a manticore doesn't mean that they ever expect to see one, or even think it's particularly realistic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think we are going to have to profoundly disagree. I think it takes a lot of understanding to go from &quot;hey that's alot more advanced than a Wake up Asuna Ap&quot; and you can't do that without extended interaction with it. Vs you can tell right away &quot;That's a dragon&quot; or &quot;cats don't talk&quot;<br /> <br /> I should probably go through the Drone thing on second thought. A Drone that responds to your commands and can talk back. Nothing unusual there. a Drone that can shoot weapons. Nothing unusual there. A Drone with manipulator claw, nothing outside bounds there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 02-21-2018, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:39:14-08:00","id":1188375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188374#post1188374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think we are going to have to profoundly disagree. I think it takes a lot of understanding to go from &quot;hey that's alot more advanced than a Wake up Asuna Ap&quot; and you can't do that without extended interaction with it. Vs you can tell right away &quot;That's a dragon&quot; or &quot;cats don't talk&quot;<br /> <br /> I should probably go through the Drone thing on second thought. A Drone that responds to your commands and can talk back. Nothing unusual there. a Drone that can shoot weapons. Nothing unusual there. A Drone with manipulator claw, nothing outside bounds there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose we are. Different strokes for different folks, I guess. But then, isn't that just Mage in a nutshell? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will say, however, that a dragon is on par with a giant mech in terms of being &quot;why even bother&quot; levels of vulgar. Call me crazy (and I admit that this does sound a little loony), but I actually don't think that people would have an easier time buying a fully sentient, free-willed A.I. than they would a talking cat. Though, to be fair, I've lived in a community of tech-hating bumpkins for most of my life, so my perspective might be a little skewed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T19:50:19-08:00","id":1188382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188375#post1188375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose we are. Different strokes for different folks, I guess. But then, isn't that just Mage in a nutshell? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will say, however, that a dragon is on par with a giant mech in terms of being &quot;why even bother&quot; levels of vulgar. Call me crazy (and I admit that this does sound a little loony), but I actually don't think that people would have an easier time buying a fully sentient, free-willed A.I. than they would a talking cat. Though, to be fair, I've lived in a community of tech-hating bumpkins for most of my life, so my perspective might be a little skewed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think we also might be using different things. I rarely think if a familiar larger than a Bear. a Dragon familiar would be a small dragon. I wouldn't be letting someone take Falcor as a Familiar. I wouldn't let anyone run around with a Gundam and say that's not vulgar.<br /> <br /> And the AI thing its less I think people would be more willing to buy a fully sapient AI so much as I don't think most people could tell SIRI or Google Home, or Alexa from AI Familiar in the same sort of cases without signficant interaction. So having a full conversation with them might start getting your paradox in front of Sleepers but even then if you are talking on your phone with your AI in the phone how would anyone even know?<br /> <br /> Just like Parrots are Hax Familiars because everyone knows Parrots can talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T20:12:06-08:00","id":1188389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188382#post1188382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think we also might be using different things. I rarely think if a familiar larger than a Bear. a Dragon familiar would be a small dragon. I wouldn't be letting someone take Falcor as a Familiar. I wouldn't let anyone run around with a Gundam and say that's not vulgar.<br /> <br /> And the AI thing its less I think people would be more willing to buy a fully sapient AI so much as I don't think most people could tell SIRI or Google Home, or Alexa from AI Familiar in the same sort of cases without signficant interaction. So having a full conversation with them might start getting your paradox in front of Sleepers but even then if you are talking on your phone with your AI in the phone how would anyone even know?<br /> <br /> Just like Parrots are Hax Familiars because everyone knows Parrots can talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. A.I. are a little easier to hide because they are, by definition, immaterial. Still, I think that pop culture has done a good enough job ingraining robots into the popular consciousness as &quot;crazy sci-fi thing&quot; that most people would be pretty rattled to see an R2 unit rolling down the street.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T20:49:58-08:00","id":1188394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188382#post1188382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think we also might be using different things. I rarely think if a familiar larger than a Bear. a Dragon familiar would be a small dragon. I wouldn't be letting someone take Falcor as a Familiar. I wouldn't let anyone run around with a Gundam and say that's not vulgar.<br /> <br /> And the AI thing its less I think people would be more willing to buy a fully sapient AI so much as I don't think most people could tell SIRI or Google Home, or Alexa from AI Familiar in the same sort of cases without signficant interaction. So having a full conversation with them might start getting your paradox in front of Sleepers but even then if you are talking on your phone with your AI in the phone how would anyone even know?<br /> <br /> Just like Parrots are Hax Familiars because everyone knows Parrots can talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do familiars always have the ability to talk? Is it neccessary for their function?<br /> <br /> The example I used above, of Sango's giant sabertooth cat, couldn't talk, but otherwise seems like it could be a perfectly fine familar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T20:53:58-08:00","id":1188395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188394#post1188394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do familiars always have the ability to talk? Is it neccessary for their function?<br /> <br /> The example I used above, of Sango's giant sabertooth cat, couldn't talk, but otherwise seems like it could be a perfectly fine familar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually... is a sabretooth vulgar? Would a <i>dinosaur</i> be vulgar? I'd say yes, but what do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T22:17:49-08:00","id":1188407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188395#post1188395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually... is a sabretooth vulgar? Would a <i>dinosaur</i> be vulgar? I'd say yes, but what do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it highly depends on the circumstances in which it is being presented.<br /> Some guy walking down the street with a sabretooth tiger or a dinosaur? Yeeeah, I think that would hit the familiar with the disbelief/paradox effect.<br /> <br /> However, there have been so many actual RL stories about scientists having the concrete idea of cloning these old critters from DNA found in fossils and frozen mammoths and what have you, that if a technomancer (or a mage simply pretending to be one) invited members of the public for a BIG REVEAL, and then showed off the critters along with explanations of cloning, they actually could become coincidental - even for further mages following up with the idea.<br /> <br /> Naturally the Technocracy would either send out the NWO to either suddenly 'debunk' the 'hoax' the media fell for, putting the coincidence back towards vulgarity....or the Progenitors might actually go 'Oh well, it's a slight, uncontrolled timetable acceleration. Put down regulations for the tech and we can make the best of this situation.' Slight timetable acceleration because, realistically, sleeper tech these days can pull off the whole feat already. Just nobody is crazy enough to clone HUGE PREHISTORIC BEINGS yet. Looking at you, Etherites.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T22:30:56-08:00","id":1188409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188395#post1188395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually... is a sabretooth vulgar? Would a <i>dinosaur</i> be vulgar? I'd say yes, but what do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that particular cat transforms from kitten sized to smilodon size in a billow of flame and can fly, so that one definitely would be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A normal saber toothed cat...I don't know. I think books/movies like Jurassic Park and all the news stories about cloning Mammoths may have moved it into the concidental zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T22:48:22-08:00","id":1188412,"title":"","content":"Wow. Looks like you guys think way more highly of sleepers than I do. I tend to think of them as, by default, boring sods that reject anything that interrupts their boring sod life. (Though, given the interpretation that they will accept things that they think are merely possible, rather than likely, I stand by the idea that the Choristers, Templars, Batini and other major religion based Mages should be in a more favorable position than they are in the canon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T00:49:22-08:00","id":1188431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188412#post1188412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Looks like you guys think way more highly of sleepers than I do. I tend to think of them as, by default, boring sods that reject anything that interrupts their boring sod life. (Though, given the interpretation that they will accept things that they think are merely possible, rather than likely, I stand by the idea that the Choristers, Templars, Batini and other major religion based Mages should be in a more favorable position than they are in the canon.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends how far on the sliding scale of sinicism you wish to go.<br /> <br /> For me, a sleeper is just people, the people you meet on you\u2019re normal walk to work, the guy at the bus station, the girl standing by the atm, waiting their turn. I reject the overtly consumerist portrayal that the original books used to describe sleepers as rather unfair. I also find it a bit reductionist to just say \u201conly mages, or at the very least sorcerors are capable of abstract thinking and emotive reasoning. Sleepers only do as their told, buy stuff, and watch tv.\u201d<br /> I don\u2019t mind that being a stereotype in game, especially one held by overtly snobbish mages, but to make that a reality of the setting in many ways cheapens it.<br /> <br /> For me, the only thing that separates the sleeper from the mage is that the sleeper does not believe themselves capable of magic. They are still people with their own stories and lives, every bit as complex as any mage. They may be rebellious, intellectual, imaginative, curious, and even politically charged, with their own goals and ambitions every bit as varied as a mages. Perhaps one wishes to be an astronaut, perhaps another is working up the nerve to ask the barista out, and maybe yet another is trying to get their novel published.<br /> <br /> They are simply unaware of their influence on reality, they see themselves as predominantly reactionary. Unable to change what the universe gives them, or at the very most, only able to change things with expert advice, be it spiritual, scientific, financial or otherwise.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s not forget though, that while the technocracy might have a strong hold over the consensus, it is the sleepers that actually create the consensus. If enough of them believed that pigs can genuinely fly, then they would. If enough thought they could walk through walls, then that too would be possible. The problem is that sleepers are so varied in their beliefs, that any one individual belief that differs from the main consensus is not strong enough to bring about change, that\u2019s what mages do. However, if enough people believe something, then it changes, gradually, but certainly. That is how the technocracy operates, gradual change in the guise of \u201cdevelopment\u201d in order to change the consensus little by little to something iterative enough to make individual will working unnecessary. Why awaken when everyone can do powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 02-22-2018, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T05:20:59-08:00","id":1188467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188407#post1188407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, there have been so many actual RL stories about scientists having the concrete idea of cloning these old critters from DNA found in fossils and frozen mammoths and what have you, that if a technomancer (or a mage simply pretending to be one) invited members of the public for a BIG REVEAL, and then showed off the critters along with explanations of cloning, they actually could become coincidental - even for further mages following up with the idea.<br /> <br /> Naturally the Technocracy would either send out the NWO to either suddenly 'debunk' the 'hoax' the media fell for, putting the coincidence back towards vulgarity....or the Progenitors might actually go 'Oh well, it's a slight, uncontrolled timetable acceleration. Put down regulations for the tech and we can make the best of this situation.' Slight timetable acceleration because, realistically, sleeper tech these days can pull off the whole feat already. Just nobody is crazy enough to clone HUGE PREHISTORIC BEINGS yet. Looking at you, Etherites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially skeptic sleepers are going to show to such a demonstration by their own free will if you present the reveal to the public.<br /> <br /> Namely, anyone that's interested in science, DNA and dinosaurs it's going to be there with a smirk to debunk the obvious *hoax* w/o NWO moving a finger (as they, mundane experts that they are, know that it's *impossible* to produce a working dinosaur clone now - but will be interested nevertheless). Your technobable about cloning has to be harder than adamantium (and without any trace of mad science) if you want *them* to buy it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you could try to pass them as animatronic - a hoax to be sure, but a harmless one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T05:45:50-08:00","id":1188473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188467#post1188467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially skeptic sleepers are going to show to such a demonstration by their own free will if you present the reveal to the public.<br /> <br /> Namely, anyone that's interested in science, DNA and dinosaurs it's going to be there with a smirk to debunk the obvious *hoax* w/o NWO moving a finger (as they, mundane experts that they are, know that it's *impossible* to produce a working dinosaur clone now - but will be interested nevertheless). Your technobable about cloning has to be harder than adamantium (and without any trace of mad science) if you want *them* to buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Technically the only thing you need to convince them of, is how you got your hands on dinosaur DNA that wasn't too damaged. It's pretty much the only thing that really prevents cloning a dinosaur right now (aside of, hopefully, the sanity of people with the means to do it...). There were recent hopes of finding good DNA in mosquitoes preserved in amber, but the dino DNA inside was too degraded for use.<br /> <br /> Once you have the DNA and grow a fetus in a test tube, all that's left is finding a fitting host to let it grow inside of.<br /> <br /> ...RL sleeper tech is scarier than it used to be in the 90's Mage, for sure &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-22-2018, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T06:51:15-08:00","id":1188491,"title":"","content":"Yup, harder said than done though, the mosquito thing it's pretty old - like Jurassic Park old. Healthy DNA samples aren't easy to come by.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/How_to_Clone_a_Mammoth\" target=\"_blank\">How went the effort to clone mammoths found encased in ice?</a>. You will have to justify that the DNA samples are either wholy sane or compatible enough with current fauna to produce a working clone - you're going to deal with VERY critic people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-22-2018, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T08:44:16-08:00","id":1188527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188491#post1188491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, harder said than done though, the mosquito thing it's pretty old - like Jurassic Park old. Healthy DNA samples aren't easy to come by.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/How_to_Clone_a_Mammoth\" target=\"_blank\">How went the effort to clone mammoths found encased in ice?</a>. You will have to justify that the DNA samples are either wholy sane or compatible enough with current fauna to produce a working clone - you're going to deal with VERY critic people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely, that's a given.<br /> I'm just saying that the majority of effort will need to be put into explaining how the hell you got the genetic material in the first place, moreso than how the cloning actually worked. Prepared (faked or real) paperwork will need preparation, you should better be able to show off an actual lab you supposedly did it in (or cleverly put morally-dark effort into making some existing lab staff believe that it happened at theirs...) etc. etc.<br /> <br /> In other words, you need to make full use of the path that the Techocracy paved for you. It certainly isn't a thing that a Mage is going to do to get people *away* from the Technocratic paradigm..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T10:22:32-08:00","id":1188560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188389#post1188389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair. A.I. are a little easier to hide because they are, by definition, immaterial. Still, I think that pop culture has done a good enough job ingraining robots into the popular consciousness as &quot;crazy sci-fi thing&quot; that most people would be pretty rattled to see an R2 unit rolling down the street.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can buy and people DO make R2 units for cons. Maybe when it starts showing off a full range of &quot;Does everything it can in the movies&quot; people are going to call the bluff but if its just rolling around out there its nothing a sleeper can't get with a toy. My general rule of thumb is technomancers get &quot;a bit beyond cutting edge&quot; tech as within coincidence for the price of not being able to give up their tools early.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188394#post1188394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do familiars always have the ability to talk? Is it neccessary for their function?<br /> <br /> The example I used above, of Sango's giant sabertooth cat, couldn't talk, but otherwise seems like it could be a perfectly fine familar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking is bought, you can have a normalish hyper intelligent cat who has to communicate as a normalish cat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188395#post1188395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually... is a sabretooth vulgar? Would a <i>dinosaur</i> be vulgar? I'd say yes, but what do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the Sabertooth tiger would be able to pass as a normal big cat for most people, even the sabertooth could just be seen as a wierd mutation on a big cat.<br /> <br /> Dinosaurs.. it really depends. If you want a Utahraptor or bigger... vulgar. IF you want something the size of a turkey I'd let it pass as &quot;its just a wierd bird&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T10:36:54-08:00","id":1188566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188412#post1188412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Looks like you guys think way more highly of sleepers than I do. I tend to think of them as, by default, boring sods that reject anything that interrupts their boring sod life. (Though, given the interpretation that they will accept things that they think are merely possible, rather than likely, I stand by the idea that the Choristers, Templars, Batini and other major religion based Mages should be in a more favorable position than they are in the canon.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Familiars aren't covered by the same scale as other magics. They either get a point of paradox because someone observes something off.. or they don't. A dragon who no one ever sees never gets hit with Paradox. So someone who takes Puff the Magic Dragon(who is invisible!) is never going to get hit with paradox from it.<br /> <br /> I make it rather HARD for familiars to get you Paradox as getting rid of Paradox is their primary purpose, it needs to be the most horribly obviously blatant thing: a cat talking, a bird made of fire etc. Technology is generally a good disguise in my mind for alot of leeway but I'm also probably going to give the benefit of the doubt to the person who is trying to keep their dragon hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T14:26:20-08:00","id":1188662,"title":"","content":"Minor nitpick: FiDF lets you get 1 dox per dot in the familiar background if your familiar is acting vulgar (or just be there in clear sight in case of a giant mount of scaly firebreathing dragonness).<br /> <br /> I once had a small gnome/earth spirit/elemental as a Familiar. Most of the time he was wearing kids clothes and a Halloween mask.<br /> <br /> I found the rare occasion that earned me dox well worth the benefit of having him.<br /> He had elemental immunity and as such was rather unimpressed by bullets.<br /> <br /> Another Familiar was a symbiont. A formless black ooze that bonded with my skin, not unlike the one spiderman had.<br /> That went rather well because of circumstances. Most of the time the antagonists were completely supernatural (vampire crossover).<br /> So for the familiar going full on vulgar was not an issue.<br /> <br /> I think if you already have a means of getting rid of dox it is a small price to pay for style to have a bygone or other blatantly supernatural being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T16:06:07-08:00","id":1188691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188467#post1188467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially skeptic sleepers are going to show to such a demonstration by their own free will if you present the reveal to the public.<br /> <br /> Namely, anyone that's interested in science, DNA and dinosaurs it's going to be there with a smirk to debunk the obvious *hoax* w/o NWO moving a finger (as they, mundane experts that they are, know that it's *impossible* to produce a working dinosaur clone now - but will be interested nevertheless). Your technobable about cloning has to be harder than adamantium (and without any trace of mad science) if you want *them* to buy it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you could try to pass them as animatronic - a hoax to be sure, but a harmless one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dinosaur yeah, but with Pleistocene megafauna it's easy to explain where you got the DNA. We found a body frozen in the permafrost and were able to get a great scan of their DNA.<br /> <br /> The Denisovan genome is sequenced to a quality equal to genomes sequenced of living people today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 02-22-2018, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T08:13:12-08:00","id":1188876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188691#post1188691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dinosaur yeah, but with Pleistocene megafauna it's easy to explain where you got the DNA. We found a body frozen in the permafrost and were able to get a great scan of their DNA.<br /> <br /> The Denisovan genome is sequenced to a quality equal to genomes sequenced of living people today.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you can clone a Mammoth without mixing the stuff with elephant DNA? I'm not an expert, I just know what I've heard, that 's why I ask. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T14:34:22-08:00","id":1189012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1188876#post1188876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you can clone a Mammoth without mixing the stuff with elephant DNA? I'm not an expert, I just know what I've heard, that 's why I ask. </div> </div> </div> </div>I think you would use crisper to edit an elephants dna to be identical to a mammoth. Then replace the dna in an elephant ovum with that. Do the same thing with a sperm cell (using a different mammoth sequence). In vitro fertilization and then implant the embryo in a female elephant. <br /> <br /> This is easier if we develop artificial wombs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T22:56:12-08:00","id":1189123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188322-anyone-had-a-bygone-familiar-how-did-it-work-out?p=1189012#post1189012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you would use crisper to edit an elephants dna to be identical to a mammoth. Then replace the dna in an elephant ovum with that. Do the same thing with a sperm cell (using a different mammoth sequence). In vitro fertilization and then implant the embryo in a female elephant.<br /> <br /> This is easier if we develop artificial wombs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that.<br /> CRISPR is one of the very new ( as in, just a couple of years old ) developments of genetic engineering; Without going into too much detail, imagine a revolutionarily and extremely cost-effective way of editing the Genome or RNA of living cells in very precise and very specific ways - including in fully grown organisms. In the latter case, the application is literally an injection.<br /> <br /> Though right now it is majorly being used to modify specific genes of the DNA inside eggs or fetuses for experimentation, and there are of course trials and experimentation going on - a lot of it. Because this thing might be very big one day; We literally have the technology in our hands that could remove a genetic disease from patients with a mere injection sooner or later.<br /> <br /> Or, if you want an example, a current procedure that some scientists are doing kind of 'for-fun' (with the goal of learning) is making various animals that glow in the dark under a specific light. We're talking pigs and cats here, not fungi. Usually, right now, by CRISPRing up the fetuses before they grow.<br /> And the newest idea that's making the rounds is growing human organs inside pigs for transplants. Not just any organs. organs with the transplant patient's own DNA.<br /> <br /> And just to fully drive the point home about how much CRISPR is a revolution - remember those 'my first chemistry' set things you could buy to reproduce little fun chemistry experiments at home?<br /> ....there are CRISPR kits like that. You can, literally, buy the equivalent of 'My first CRISPR kit' and do a series of genetic modification experiments of bacteria and the like at home.<br /> And so-called BioHackers have taken the dangerous path of making their own CRISPR payloads and self-experimentation.<br /> <br /> The Progenitors are going wild, I'm telling you.<br /> Several things that were utterly vulgar in the early Mage days? They are heading straight for coincidence at a scary pace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-24-2018, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}